  "synonym_discrimination": null,
  "usage_note": "**In the south of** a place means inside it (*in the south of the country*); **to the south of** a place means outside it, beyond its southern edge (*the hills to the south of the town*). The noun nearly always takes **the**; for *drive south*, without **the**, see the adverb.",
